# Originally converted from sike_sandals.glb by tools/models/glb_tool.py.
# ⚠️ THAT TOOL NO LONGER EXISTS IN THE REPO, so this file is now maintained by hand.
# Re-running the converter would reintroduce the bug below; edit here instead.
#
# ⚠️ m2 IS THE SHOE BODY AND ITS Kd MUST NOT GO BACK TO 0 0 0.
# The source GLB ships baseColorFactor [0,0,0,1] on both body materials and carries no
# textures at all, so the converter faithfully wrote pure black. A pure-black albedo
# returns nothing under the toon key light: every curve on the upper resolves to the same
# value and the shoe renders as a flat silhouette with the m3 swoosh floating on top.
# That is the "IKE is corrupted" report. The mesh itself is clean (33,856 unique
# positions, 0 degenerate faces, normals and UVs present) so the geometry needs nothing.
#
# 0.0400/0.0446/0.0569, FROM 0.052/0.058/0.074 ON 2026-08-29, AND THE THIRD TIME OF ASKING.
# 🧑, three times in two sittings: "make sike darker too", "sike/ike still aint dark enough",
# and off the character screen, "this is what im saying wtf is this its so light",
# "ike in character select should be darker btw not white".
#
# ⚠️⚠️ HALVING IT TWICE BARELY MOVED THE PIXEL, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE REASON IT KEPT COMING BACK.
# THIS NUMBER IS CONSUMED AS LINEAR, NOT AS sRGB. The project is Linear
# (ProjectSettings m_ActiveColorSpace: 1), and measured through the character screen with
# ModelPreviewProbe, a Kd of 0.052 renders at 89/255 with the ink outline off the mean. That is
# the arithmetic of a LINEAR reflectance: 0.052 x 1.35 key = 0.070 linear, which encodes to
# sRGB 0.294 = 75/255, and the measured darkest decile was 74. Not a coincidence.
#
# So the intuition that produced 0.105 -> 0.052 was reading these as display values, where
# halving black-ish gets you blacker. In linear they are reflectances, and halving 0.105 to 0.052
# moves the SCREEN value only from about 92/255 to about 75/255: still a mid grey, which is
# exactly what he photographed and exactly why two rounds of halving did not answer it.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ 0.0400 IS BISECTED ON THE RENDER, NOT SOLVED ON PAPER, AND THE PAPER ANSWER WAS WRONG BY
# A LOT. The first attempt at this reasoned forward through the grade, assumed it LIFTS the low
# end, and landed on 0.0070. Measured through ModelPreviewProbe, 0.0070 renders the shoe at a
# mean of 0,0,5: pure black, the exact failure the floor below exists to prevent, arrived at by
# arithmetic that looked careful. ColourGrade CRUSHES the toe rather than lifting it — the same
# `lerp(0.5, c, contrast)` behaviour IlalimNgTulayBuilder works out at length for that map, where
# every linear pixel below a threshold clips to zero before it reaches the screen.
#
# So it is measured instead, on the character screen, with the flat skin in place:
#
#     Kd 0.0800  ->  mean  87
#     Kd 0.0550  ->  mean  63
#     Kd 0.0400  ->  mean  43  THE VALUE SHIPPED HERE: dark, form still readable
#     Kd 0.0280  ->  mean  22
#     Kd 0.0200  ->  mean   0  (black, no form left)
#
# ⚠️⚠️ AND THE LADDER WAS SWEPT TWICE, BECAUSE THE FIRST SWEEP WAS TAKEN UNDER THE WRONG LIGHTS.
# It ran while ModelPreview.LightExposure was still 1.0, and answered 0.0180. The character screen
# was at that point lit 1.54x hotter than every map in the game (docs/TODO.md § 79.1), and once
# that was corrected to 0.651 the same 0.0180 rendered at mean 0: pure black. **A value bisected
# against the wrong lighting is not a value.** The ladder above is the re-sweep, and it is the one
# that matches what ships. The old readings, for the record, were 0.0520 -> 111 (his screenshot,
# "so light"), 0.0300 -> 73, 0.0180 -> 44.
#
# The two other channels keep the original 1 : 1.115 : 1.423 ratio so the shoe stays the same
# faintly cool near-black it was authored as.
#
# ⚠️ MEASURED AFTER THE FLAT SKIN LANDED, NOT BEFORE, AND THE ORDER MATTERS. ToonSkin.ApplySlipper
# raises the toon shadow band from 0.45 to 0.86 for tsinelas only, so the shoe no longer has a
# darkened half to hide in: the albedo now carries essentially all of the value. Measured on the
# same probe, the flat skin alone took this shoe from a mean of 89 to 111. Re-deriving this Kd
# against the OLD shading would put it back to grey.
#
# ⚠️ THE OLD NUMBER'S REASONING WAS NOT WRONG, ITS CONDITIONS CHANGED. It was measured as
# "the darkest the body can sit and still separate the toe box from the midsole" against a
# 0.012 m prop ink border. That border is 0.006 m as of the same day (ToonSkin.PropOutlineWidth,
# docs/TODO.md § 78.7), so twice as much of the shoe's own shading is now visible and the
# separation it was protecting no longer depends on the albedo being that light.
#
# ⚠️ STILL NOT ZERO, AND IT MUST NOT GO THERE. The floor is the original bug: a pure black
# albedo returns nothing under the toon key light, every curve resolves to one value, and the
# shoe becomes a flat silhouette with the m3 swoosh floating on it. That is the "IKE is
# corrupted" report and 0 0 0 is what caused it. This is dark, not black.
newmtl m2
Kd 0.04000 0.04460 0.05690
Ks 0.14000 0.14000 0.16000
Ns 48.00000
d 1.00000
illum 2
newmtl m3
Kd 0.94000 0.94000 0.93000
Ks 0.08000 0.08000 0.08000
Ns 24.00000
d 1.00000
illum 2
